## No other test renders a genuinely asymmetric partial sphere's image.
## transforms.rib's Sphere 0.5 -0.5 0.5 360 is a full sphere (zmin =
## -radius, zmax = radius) and proves nothing about
## GMANSphere::getLocation's zmin/zmax parameterization. This one -- zmin
## = -0.5, zmax = radius = 1 -- is asymmetric: a cap is missing, a
## hemisphere is not.
##
## Explicit Clipping, not the RI_EPSILON-near default: this shape hits a
## general near-clip precision defect (see AGENTS.md's "Near-clip precision
## at the default Clipping"), same as a camera-facing Disk.
Display "partial_sphere.tif" "file" "rgba"
Format 200 200 1
Projection "perspective" "fov" [45]
Clipping 0.5 50
Translate 0 0 5
WorldBegin
	LightSource "ambientlight" 1 "intensity" [0.6]
	Sides 1
	Surface "matte" "Ka" [1] "Kd" [0]
	Sphere 1 -0.5 1 360
WorldEnd
